course: dictionary
lesson: 15963
title: Words that do not travel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have no exact match in another language. We call them untranslatable. «The Danish word hygge is hard to translate into English.» You can explain what it means, but a single English word will not fit it exactly.
explain: An explanation can be long, but it may lose some of the feeling. «Hygge» means cosy togetherness, the warm feeling of sitting with friends by candlelight. A long explanation can describe that feeling, yet the short, friendly sound of the word is lost when you translate it.
explain: Jokes and puns are often untranslatable too. «The pun worked in English, but it was untranslatable into French.» The joke depends on words that sound alike in English, so it may not make anyone laugh in another language. When a word is only partly translatable, we can call it almost untranslatable.
fact: Untranslatable means it has no exact match in another language.
fact: You can often explain an untranslatable word, but the explanation may be long and lose some feeling.
fact: «Hygge» (Danish) means cosy togetherness.
fact: «Saudade» (Portuguese) means a sad longing, often for someone or something far away.
fact: A pun or joke can be untranslatable when its fun depends on the sounds or meanings of one language.
exercise: What does untranslatable mean? | *No exact match in another language | Written in a very old book | Spelled with many letters | Easy to read aloud
exercise: «The Danish word hygge is untranslatable.» Why is «hygge» hard to translate? | It is an English word | It means very cold | It is a long number | *It has no exact match in English
exercise: «Her joke was an untranslatable pun, so the French audience did not laugh.» What does this tell you about the pun? | It was told in a loud voice | It was written in French | It was very short | *Some of its fun is lost when it is translated
test: «Saudade» is a Portuguese word for a sad longing. Why might a translation lose something? | *The feeling is hard to fit into one English word | Translations never use feelings | Saudade is a number | Portuguese words are always shorter
test: Which of these is an example of an almost untranslatable thing? | The number seven | A red chair | *A pun that depends on sounds in one language | A cold glass of water
exam: «A translator said hygge is untranslatable.» What does the translator mean? | Hygge is only a number | *There is no single English word that carries the same warm feeling | Hygge is an English word that is hard to spell | Hygge cannot be spoken aloud
